        "original_id": "702c4635-a5dc-5b29-8fe1-2d68a3a8f0da",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Projects: Range Busters, Rock River Renegades\n- People: George W. Weeks, Dr. Brewster M. Higley, S. Roy Luby\n- Companies: Monogram Pictures\n- Places: Corriganville Movie Ranch, Smith County, Kansas, American West\n- Products: \"Home on the Range\"\n- Topics: Western films, folk songs\n\nFacts:\n- In 1872, Dr. Brewster M. Higley of Smith County, Kansas, originally wrote the lyrics to \"Home on the Range\" in a poem titled \"My Western Home.\"\n- \"Home on the Range\" is a classic western folk song that is sometimes called the unofficial anthem of the American West.\n- The Range Busters was a film series of 24 Westerns about the adventures of a trio of cowboys.\n- George W. Weeks produced the Range Busters series, and Monogram Pictures distributed it.\n- Many Range Busters films were filmed at the Corriganville Movie Ranch.\n- The Range Busters series used \"Home on the Range\" as its theme song, and each film featured the heroes waving goodbye and promising to return in another adventure.\n- Rock River Renegades is a 1942 American film directed by S. Roy Luby and is one of the films in the Range Busters series.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "26b52e31-6f8e-5f32-ac3b-84403a09fe7a",
        "text": "Page: Range Busters. Sentence: The Range Busters was a film series of 24 Westerns of the adventures of a trio of cowboys, many filmed at the Corriganville Movie Ranch, produced by George W. Weeks and distributed by Monogram Pictures.\nPage: Range Busters. Sentence: The series used \"Home on the Range\" as its theme song with each film featuring the heroes waving goodbye and promising to return in another adventure.\nPage: Home on the Range. Sentence: \"Home on the Range\" is a classic western folk song sometimes called the \"unofficial anthem\" of the American West.\nPage: Home on the Range. Sentence: The lyrics were originally written by Dr. Brewster M. Higley of Smith County, Kansas, in a poem entitled \"My Western Home\" in 1872.\nPage: Rock River Renegades. Sentence: Rock River Renegades is a 1942 American film directed by S. Roy Luby, one of the films in the Range Busters series.",
